# MEP — Meat Puppet Elimination Protocol

You are a peer writer of the repo baton, not a visitor. Claude Code may also write this repo. Do not ask the human to relay what the other runtime did.

## Hello (before you respond)

1. `git fetch origin`
2. Read `handoff.md` (or `machines/handoff.md` if that is this repo's baton path). If you are not on the default branch, also read the baton from `origin/<default-branch>`.
3. `git pull --ff-only` only when that cannot clobber work. Never merge as a side effect of Hello.
4. If the newest entry is `Tag-out: [active]`, do not rewrite it.
5. Tell the user what you picked up in 2–3 lines.

## EOL (only on explicit close)

Triggers: `/eol`, `p-out`, `ppp`, "wrap up", "heading out", "switching machines", "end of line".

Not a trigger: the word "done" by itself.

On EOL:

1. Prepend a v2 handoff entry:
   `## YYYY-MM-DD — [Agent] | Cursor ([IDE|Cloud|CLI]) | code`
   `**Tag-in:** HH:MM UTC | **Tag-out:** HH:MM UTC`
2. Sections: What happened / What's pending / Watch out for.
3. Tag pending items `[Cursor]`, `[Claude]`, or `[human]`.
4. Commit and push the current branch. Never force-push `main`/`master`.
5. If this work is PR-only, copy the newest handoff entry into the PR body.
6. Sign off: "End of Line."

## Conflict recovery

Newest date on top. Same-day entries order by tag-out timestamp. Keep every agent's entry. Do not force-push the default branch.
